  "text": "Farag et al. analyzed 32 tumor studies on the HALP score, reporting it as an independent risk factor for poor prognosis and tumor grading or differentiation [30]. In that review, the median score across subtypes was 31.2, higher in gastric cancer (56.8) and adenocarcinoma (44.56), lower in colorectal (26.5) and bladder (22.2) cancer. Although no threshold is universally valid, low HALP scores significantly predicted poor outcome in intergroup comparisons in most cancers [6, 31–36]. In our study the median was 23.35, again reflecting this heterogeneity, and it was significantly lower in non-survivors at 30-day and 1-year mortality."
